    <origin>Owner round 95 (notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md). Contract notes/ontology-standard-child-contract-2026-10-12.md §3 C4 and C7, §4 "unified-access-control-r2" items 1-2. Audit notes/ontology-secure-schema-audit-2026-10-12.md F4.</origin>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement UAC's items 1-2 of the child-record contract on the ontology integration branch, then open a PR INTO `docs/ontology-platform-design`, not master. Read the contract note and the audit's F4 first. Do not change any ontology writer: those are ontology tasks 141-145.</prompt>

  <goal>(1) BRANCH. Create a fresh worktree from `origin/docs/ontology-platform-design` on a new branch `uac/182-ontology-lineage-census`. The PR's base is `docs/ontology-platform-design`. The ontology main session merges it; you never merge it.

(2) LINEAGE (C4). In `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Access/SecureChildLineage.cs`, the `sprk_decisionrecord` row gains the 8 subject lookups now live on spaarkedev1 (ontology task 140): `sprk_regarding{communication,document,event,invoice,matter,project,todo,workassignment}`. Use the existing `Regarding(...)` helper, as the `sprk_signal` row does.
- KEEP the existing typed `sprk_matter`, `sprk_project` and `sprk_workassignment` entries. Contract C2 says they leave only after ontology task 145's backfill is verified.
- EXCLUDE `sprk_regardingservicerequest`, the same as Signal's row; a service request cannot be secure.
- Update the row's comment with the source: live 2026-10-12, task 140 / #1763.

(3) CENSUS CHILD TABLES (C7, F4). In `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs`, add `sprk_signal`, `sprk_decisionrecord` and `sprk_budgetrevision` to `ChildTables`.
- Every create of those tables that the scanner then finds gets a `CensusEntry` that tells the truth about the code AT THE BRANCH HEAD.
  - A create that resolves its owner through `IRecordOwnershipResolver` is `Routed`.
  - A create that does not yet is `Waived` with `WaiverKind.Pending`, naming the ontology task that routes it: 142 for the Decision Record writer, 143 for SignalWriter's no-core and D-130 owner.
- Follow the file's maintenance procedure exactly. Never mark something `Routed` that is not, and never `Permanent`.

(4) CONSISTENCY GUARD (C7). A new source-only ArchTest (no DI, no network; ADR-038 B3) asserting that three sets agree:
- every table in `SecureChildLineage.Children`;
- every table in `config/secure-record-owner-role.json` `tables[]` whose `kind` is `child`;
- every table in the census `ChildTables` that is a lineage child.

Specifically:
- A table in lineage but not in the role config fails.
- A table in the role config (kind child) but not in lineage fails.
- A lineage table missing from `ChildTables` fails.
- Tables that are deliberately in one set and not another are allow-listed, with a reason per entry.
- It needs a negative control proving it fires.

(5) DIRECT OWNINGBUSINESSUNIT WRITES (F4). Extend the census so a write of the `owningbusinessunit` attribute (a literal or const key) in `src/server` fails unless it is listed. List today's sites truthfully; the audit F2 SignalWriter site goes as Pending against task 143. Add a negative control. Use the existing owner-write census (`OwnerWriteEntry`) shape if it fits, rather than a new mechanism (CLAUDE.md §11).</goal>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Extend the existing census and SourceScan helpers. Add no new framework.</constraint>
    <constraint source="contract">No change to any ontology writer, the resolver, CoreAncestorResolver or the restamper. Those are ontology tasks 141-145, and UAC reviews them separately.</constraint>
    <constraint source="git">Stage explicit paths only. Never force-push, never bare `git stash`, never `--no-verify`. Do not merge the PR, and do not touch master.</constraint>
    <constraint source="machine">The machine is shared and loaded. Kill only your own PIDs, never by image name.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/ontology-standard-child-contract-2026-10-12.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/ontology-secure-schema-audit-2026-10-12.md</file>
