      <file>config/secure-record-owner-role.json (howToExtend)</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Worktree from origin/docs/ontology-platform-design; read the contract C4/C7 and the census header.</step>
    <step>Lineage row; ChildTables; the census entries the scanner now demands, with truthful dispositions.</step>
    <step>Consistency guard and owningbusinessunit detection, each with a negative control.</step>
    <step>Build the BFF; run Spaarke.ArchTests in full, plus SecureChildLineage, SecureChildReconciler and SecureChildShareSynchronizer unit tests. Open the PR into docs/ontology-platform-design and report counts.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A create or owner write on these tables that you cannot classify truthfully: STOP and report the site.</trigger>
    <trigger>The consistency guard finds a disagreement between lineage, the role config and the census that is not obviously an allow-list case: STOP and list it. Do not "fix" the role config. Role privilege changes are recorded as refusal first, per howToExtend, and the owner decides.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>The DR lineage row lists the 8 subject lookups and keeps the three typed core lookups. servicerequest is absent (a unit test pins this).</criterion>
    <criterion>ChildTables contains sprk_signal, sprk_decisionrecord and sprk_budgetrevision. The census passes at the branch head, with every new entry's disposition matching the code.</criterion>
    <criterion>The consistency guard passes at the head and fails in its negative control. It also fails if a lineage table is removed from the role config, demonstrated once.</criterion>
    <criterion>An unlisted `owningbusinessunit` write fails the census (negative control). The listed sites are truthful.</criterion>
    <criterion>Spaarke.ArchTests: all pass. The BFF build has 0 errors. The PR targets docs/ontology-platform-design.</criterion>
    <criterion>Test scope: the cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>
</task>
